 "_doc": {
  "what": "Paying customers = distinct LOYVERSE_MERCHANT_ID with at least one subscription in status 'active' or 'non_renewing' in CHARGEBEE_SUBSCRIPTIONS_V. This is the figure Alex reports and is the headline number on the dashboard.",
  "monthClose": "One frozen value per month end. Written once and NEVER overwritten - a month close that moves is not a close. Sources: 'Alex' = taken from his own reporting; 'rebuilt' = reconstructed by paying_customers_backfill.sql; 'snapshot' = captured live by the daily step in run.py.",
  "daily": "A live reading per day from paying_customers_active_subs.sql. On days 1-3 of a month the earliest of these becomes the previous month's close if it has none.",
  "rebuiltAdjustment": "The backfill runs -50 against its raw result. That offset was measured, not guessed: with it, all four months you had already rebuilt (2025-12 to 2026-03) and 2026-10 reproduce EXACTLY, and Alex's own six months (2026-04 to 2026-09) land within -3 to +7, mean +0.2. Checked 2026-11-09.",
  "whyRebuiltIsApproximate": "Before 2026-11 nobody was snapshotting this daily, so history is reconstructed from subscription lifecycle dates crossed with invoice coverage. It cannot be exact and is not claimed to be."
 },
